# Modular Architecture (Core)

Project follows layered **Clean Architecture**. Reference existing modules (`Login`, `Document`) when adding features.

## Module Layout

```
domain/{feature}/     — UseCase, domain model, mapper, di/Module.kt
data/{feature}/       — Api, DTO, RemoteDataSource, RepositoryImpl, di/Module.kt
database/             — Room entity, DAO, LocalDataSource, DbRepository
```

## Rules

- One **domain module** per business feature (`domain/auth`, `domain/document`, `domain/category`)
- Database and remote access live in **separate modules**, not inside domain
- Copy structure from an existing feature before inventing a new layout

## Do / Don't

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — business logic + HTTP in composeApp
class LoginViewModel(private val ktor: HttpClient) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — feature split across layers
// domain/auth/usecase/GetLoginUseCase.kt
// data/auth/repository/LoginRepositoryImpl.kt
// database/repository/LoginDbRepositoryImpl.kt
```
